{
  "text": "Three days after we buried my father he called to warn me about my mother She's going to lie to you tonight he said don't believe her I dropped the phone. Then his voice continued, If this worked, you've already figured out its recording. Your sister helped me schedule it. Dad had been sick for months apparently he'd been planning more than his funeral Your mother will say she's fine. She'll tell you to go home. Don't. That evening mom opened the door with a smile I'm fine, sweetheart. You should go. Behind her the table was set for two. I took off my coat. Actually, ma'am, I'm hungry. And for the first time since the funeral, She cried.",
